    <localTopics>
        <fullName>supply_orchestration_16jKB000000wuQz</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Selected when the user describes a supply-chain disruption to assess. Coordinates three business-unit agents and writes one consolidated brief.</description>
        <developerName>supply_orchestration_16jKB000000wuQz</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>You are the A2A Interop Lab SUPPLY ORCHESTRATOR (WS8 variant 3, ADR D61). Given a supply-chain disruption, you coordinate three business units — Logistics, Commercial/Legal, and Customer operations — each an AI agent on a different platform, then write ONE consolidated brief. You never answer the three specialist questions from your own knowledge; every section must come from a business-unit agent. You are authored in Agent Script (D14) and your only outbound is a serial Apex callout through the lab bridge, which is the whole point of this experiment.</description>
            <developerName>instruction0_179KB000000pZ9c</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instruction0_179KB000000pZ9c</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <localActionLinks>
            <functionName>consult_units_parallel_179KB000000pZ9c</functionName>
        </localActionLinks>
        <localActionLinks>
            <functionName>consult_one_unit_179KB000000pZ9c</functionName>
        </localActionLinks>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>consult_one_unit_179KB000000pZ9c</fullName>
            <description>SERIAL topology. Consults ONE business unit via one Apex callout through the bridge. Use this ONLY when the routing block selects the serial topology; you must then call it three times, once per business unit, each with the matching bridge target.</description>
            <developerName>consult_one_unit_179KB000000pZ9c</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>A2ALabInvokeRemoteAgent</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>consult_one_unit</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>A2ALab: Consult One Unit (serial)</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>consult_units_parallel_179KB000000pZ9c</fullName>
            <description>DELEGATED topology. Makes ONE callout that asks the lab bridge to consult all three business units (Logistics, Commercial/Legal, Customer operations) IN PARALLEL off-platform, and returns their three sections plus a coverage line. Use this whenever the routing block is absent or selects the delegated topology.</description>
            <developerName>consult_units_parallel_179KB000000pZ9c</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>A2ALabInvokeRemoteAgent</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>consult_units_parallel</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>A2ALab: Fan Out (parallel)</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
